---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';

const CONTACT = 'business@tacticalsolutions.com';

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'The problem', href: '#problem' },
  { label: 'The loop', href: '#loop' },
  { label: 'Trust', href: '#trust' },
  { label: 'Walkthrough', href: '#walkthrough' },
];

const proofTiles = [
  'Every non-conformance captured at the machine, in under 60 seconds.',
  'CAPAs drafted autonomously. The quality lead approves, and stops authoring.',
  'Audit trail kept current in the background: ISO, FDA, customer.',
  'Built for plants and crews, not HQ.',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Weft PocketQS"
  description="Your quality system, run from a pocket. Capture a non-conformance on your phone. Weft drafts the CAPA, pulls the root cause, and keeps the audit trail current."
  canonicalPath="/weft"
  brandLabel="Weft PocketQS"
  brandHref="/weft"
  navLinks={navLinks}
  navCta={{ label: 'Book a 20-min walkthrough', href: '#walkthrough' }}
  wide
>
  <section id="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Autonomous quality operations</p>
    <h1>Your quality system, run from a pocket.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Capture a non-conformance on your phone. Weft PocketQS drafts the CAPA,
      pulls the root cause from your own event history, and keeps the audit trail
      current. Your people run the line, not the paperwork.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="#walkthrough">Book a 20-min walkthrough</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="#loop">See the loop</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-proof">
      Built by Tactical Solutions. Pre-launch: we are opening a small first cohort
      of design partners, not selling generally yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="problem">
    <h2>The 40 hours a week you don't have.</h2>
    <p>
      Most quality programmes fail the same way. Not because teams don't care.
      Because the system costs 40 hours a week of admin nobody has.
    </p>
    <p>Right now, on your floor:</p>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li>Operators jot non-conformances on a clipboard. Half never make it into the QMS.</li>
      <li>The quality lead retypes them at 5pm, guesses the cause, drafts the CAPA next week.</li>
      <li>The audit trail is a folder of PDFs nobody trusts until an auditor shows up.</li>
      <li>Continuous improvement is a slide. The actual loop, find and fix and learn, does not close.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="sub-line">
      The fix is not another QMS tab. It is removing the admin from the loop
      entirely.
    </p>
    <p class="aside-link">
      What that looks like in one deviation, hour by hour:
      <a href={withBase('/pov/non-conformance-nine-days')}>the non-conformance that takes nine days to become a number</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="loop">
    <h2>The loop.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Weft PocketQS closes the quality loop. Four steps, running in the
      background, from a phone in a pocket.
    </p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <div class="card step">
        <p class="step-num">1. Capture</p>
        <h3>At the machine, under 60 seconds.</h3>
        <p>
          The operator opens the app, points the camera, talks or types. Product,
          line, shift and cause code are extracted automatically. No forms.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card step">
        <p class="step-num">2. Triage</p>
        <h3>As it lands.</h3>
        <p>
          Severity is classified, the event routed to the right lead, and every
          related event from the last 90 days pulled in. Repeat offenders show up
          as repeat offenders, not fresh tickets.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card step">
        <p class="step-num">3. CAPA</p>
        <h3>Drafted, not authored.</h3>
        <p>
          A corrective and preventive action is written against your own playbook:
          root cause, containment, corrective, preventive, verification. The
          quality lead edits and approves. They stop being the typist.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card step">
        <p class="step-num">4. Audit trail</p>
        <h3>Always current.</h3>
        <p>
          Every event, decision, signature and attachment is logged against your
          framework: ISO 9001, IATF, FDA 21 CFR Part 820, customer-specific. When
          the auditor walks in, the binder is already built.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities">
    <h2>What Weft PocketQS handles.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Mobile capture.</h3>
        <p>Photo, video, voice, barcode, measurement. Any shift, any phone. Offline-first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>CAPA drafting.</h3>
        <p>Pulls from your SOPs, prior CAPAs and the event itself. Writes the 8D or your internal format.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Root-cause assist.</h3>
        <p>5-Why and fishbone drafted against actual event history, not a blank page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Non-conformance management.</h3>
        <p>Severity, disposition, scrap, rework, containment. Linked to batches, work orders, machines.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Document control.</h3>
        <p>SOP versioning, training attestations and redlines, tracked automatically.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Supplier NCRs.</h3>
        <p>Issue, track and close non-conformances with suppliers without another email thread.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Audit mode.</h3>
        <p>Pull any finding, any framework, any window. Export the exact packet an auditor asks for.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Integrations.</h3>
        <p>
          Target integrations for the first cohort: ERP, MES and your existing QMS
          if you have one. We meet the floor where it is.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="trust">
    <h2>Humans in the loop, where it matters.</h2>
    <p>
      Weft PocketQS does not make quality decisions alone. It does the work
      around the decision.
    </p>
    <p class="pull-line">The system drafts. Your quality lead approves.</p>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li>CAPAs are drafted, never closed autonomously.</li>
      <li>Dispositions on high-severity non-conformances always require a named signer.</li>
      <li>Every action is logged with the exact prompt, data and model version that produced it. Defensible in audit, reproducible in review.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We treat a quality system the way a regulated auditor would. If we cannot
      prove how a decision was made, we do not ship it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="proof">
    <h2>Design-partner cohort. First three slots open.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      We are opening a small first cohort before general availability. No logos
      here yet, we will swap in named references the day they close.
    </p>
    <p class="proof-status">Currently onboarding design partners.</p>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Hours saved per site, per week.</h3>
        <p class="metric-value">Tracked since day one</p>
        <p>The number that decides whether this was worth the change.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Time to first CAPA draft.</h3>
        <p class="metric-value">Tracked since day one</p>
        <p>Capture to an approved draft, measured on real captures.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Audit findings closed per cycle.</h3>
        <p class="metric-value">Tracked since day one</p>
        <p>Against your frameworks, not ours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Sites per quality lead.</h3>
        <p class="metric-value">Tracked since day one</p>
        <p>How many plants one lead can actually run.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="who-for">
    <h2>Who this is for.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Contract manufacturing, multi-site.</h3>
        <p>
          Quality and operations leaders at 50 to 500 person plants under IATF
          16949 pressure. One quality lead, three to five sites, an OEM customer
          asking for traceability you do not have time to produce. You run QS on
          clipboards, spreadsheets and a QMS you half trust. You are the one who
          stays late to close the audit packet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Regulated field service.</h3>
        <p>
          Same shape of problem under ISO 9001, FDA 21 CFR Part 820 or
          customer-audit pressure. Distributed work, an audit trail reconstructed
          after the fact, one lead covering too many sites.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">
      Probably not for a Fortune 500 plant with a 12-person QA department and a
      fully deployed enterprise QMS it is happy with. We do not replace SAP QM. We
      remove the admin around it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="pricing">
    <h2>How it is priced.</h2>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li>Per-site subscription. Priced by plant, not by seat. Operators do not pay to capture events.</li>
      <li>Design-partner pricing for the first cohort. Fixed price, fixed scope, priced to prove the loop rather than fund growth.</li>
      <li>No per-CAPA fees and no per-audit fees. Your quality system should not meter your quality system.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="sub-line">
      Numbers are quoted on a walkthrough, because they depend on sites and scope.
      Nothing is published as a price list yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      <dt>Do you replace our existing QMS?</dt>
      <dd>
        Usually no. We sit on top and close the admin loop. If your QMS is the
        bottleneck, we will tell you honestly.
      </dd>
      <dt>Can the system sign a CAPA?</dt>
      <dd>
        No. Humans sign. The system drafts, routes and keeps the record. That is
        non-negotiable in regulated environments.
      </dd>
      <dt>How does this work offline?</dt>
      <dd>
        Capture is offline-first. Events sync when the phone is back on the
        network. The floor does not wait for wifi.
      </dd>
      <dt>What frameworks do you support?</dt>
      <dd>
        ISO 9001, IATF 16949 and FDA 21 CFR Part 820 out of the box.
        Customer-specific frameworks (PPAP, APQP, your plant's internal) are
        configured per deployment.
      </dd>
      <dt>What happens to our data?</dt>
      <dd>
        Your data stays your data. We do not train shared models on customer
        quality records. Every inference is logged with the exact inputs and model
        version used.
      </dd>
      <dt>How long does a site take?</dt>
      <dd>
        That is what the first cohort measures. The commitment we are setting
        ourselves: first non-conformance captured inside a week, first drafted CAPA
        approved by the end of week two, full audit-trail coverage in 30 days.
      </dd>
      <dt>What happens to our paper records?</dt>
      <dd>
        Ingested, indexed, searchable. The back catalogue does not disappear. It
        becomes queryable.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="walkthrough">
    <h2>Book a 20-min walkthrough.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Show us one site. We show you the loop on your data, and if the fit is there
      we scope the first cohort on the same call.
    </p>
    <form id="intake" class="intake" novalidate>
      <p class="intake-intro">Six fields, one email.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-company">Company</label>
        <input id="f-company" name="company" type="text" autocomplete="organization" required />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-role">Role</label>
        <input id="f-role" name="role" type="text" autocomplete="organization-title" required />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-sites">Sites you cover</label>
        <input id="f-sites" name="sites" type="text" inputmode="numeric" required
          placeholder="How many plants?" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-qms">Current QMS</label>
        <select id="f-qms" name="qms" required>
          <option value="">Select one</option>
          <option>Paper and spreadsheets</option>
          <option>A QMS, lightly used</option>
          <option>A QMS, fully deployed</option>
          <option>Nothing yet</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-frameworks">Frameworks you are audited against</label>
        <input id="f-frameworks" name="frameworks" type="text" required
          placeholder="ISO 9001, IATF, FDA, customer-specific" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-pain">Biggest weekly time sink</label>
        <textarea id="f-pain" name="pain" rows="3" required
          placeholder="What eats the week?"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Send request</button>
        <span class="field-note">
          Opens your mail client, addressed to {CONTACT}, with these answers filled in.
        </span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <section id="final-cta">
    <h2>Your quality system should not eat your quality team.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Weft PocketQS runs it in the background so your people can run the line.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="#walkthrough">Book a 20-min walkthrough</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>Email the team</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <div class="site-footer wide">
      <p class="footer-brand">Tactical Solutions · Weft PocketQS</p>
      <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#problem">The problem</a>
        <a href="#loop">The loop</a>
        <a href="#trust">Trust</a>
        <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
        <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
        <a href="#walkthrough">Walkthrough</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="small-print">
        Weft PocketQS is built by <a href={withBase('/')}>Tactical Solutions</a>,
        the same platform behind
        <a href={withBase('/prosentinel')}>ProSentinel</a>. If you want this loop
        built into your own stack instead,
        <a href={withBase('/applied')}>Tactical Solutions Applied</a> does that.
        One autonomy layer, three go-to-markets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // v0 submission path: compose a mailto with the field values prefilled.
  // No third-party form account and no spend. Swap to a form endpoint later
  // without changing the fields.
  const form = document.getElementById('intake') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const CONTACT = 'business@tacticalsolutions.com';

  form?.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const data = new FormData(form);
    const value = (key: string) => String(data.get(key) ?? '').trim();
    const lines = [
      `Company: ${value('company')}`,
      `Role: ${value('role')}`,
      `Sites covered: ${value('sites')}`,
      `Current QMS: ${value('qms')}`,
      `Frameworks audited against: ${value('frameworks')}`,
      '',
      `Biggest weekly time sink: ${value('pain')}`,
    ];
    const subject = `Weft PocketQS walkthrough: ${value('company') || 'first cohort'}`;
    window.location.href =
      `mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(lines.join('\n'))}`;
  });
</script>

<style>
  .proof-status {
    display: inline-block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
  }
  .metric-value {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }
  .hero-proof {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .aside-link { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .sub-line { color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 60ch; }
  .footnote { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .pull-line { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .step-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .step-num {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .intake {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .intake-intro { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .field { margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .field label { font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .field input,
  .field select,
  .field textarea {
    font: inherit;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .field input:focus,
  .field select:focus,
  .field textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .field-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .faq dt { font-weight: 600; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .faq dd { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 68ch; }
  .site-footer {
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 2rem;
    max-width: 60rem;
  }
  .footer-brand { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); }
  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .footer-links a { text-decoration: none; }
  .footer-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .small-print { margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }
</style>
